# --- Dante fork: keep artifacts out of the Inferno-FPGA repo -----------------
# These were TRACKED in avb-aes3 (added before the ignore rules existed), so
# .gitignore alone did not exclude them. 159MB -> 3.9MB by dropping them from
# the initial commit. All still present on disk and in the avb-aes3 history.
sim/*.vcd
sim/*.vvp
blinky/blinky.bit
blinky/blinky.fasm
blinky/blinky.frames
blinky/blinky.json

# Phase 0.5 tooling artifacts
firmware/loader/*.o
firmware/loader/*.d
firmware/loader/loader.elf
firmware/loader/loader.elf.map
firmware/loader/loader.bin
firmware/*.img
build_seed*/
# Elke build-output: 229 MB per directory (routed json + fasm + frames). De
# build_seed*-regel hierboven dekte de dual-USB bring-up niet, die zijn dirs
# anders noemde -- vandaar het patroon op prefix in plaats van op een naam.
build_dante_*/
build_dual_*/
build_sweep/
build_sweep.log
build_usb2_*/
# Verilog-backups van tools/gen_usb_subsystem.py: de originelen zitten in de
